  "description": "Virtual Icechunk stores over ASDC TEMPO_NO2_L3 V04. The ASDC full-record snapshot (Icechunk v2, written with icechunk 2.2.2; open with icechunk >= 2.2.2) is the default. Its virtual chunk container is named 'asdc' and points at s3://asdc-prod-protected/. The ASDC manifest bucket refuses anonymous direct S3 but serves the same objects anonymously over TEA HTTPS; chunks always need Earthdata Login. To open from outside us-west-2, re-point the 'asdc' container at the TEA HTTPS alternate with a bearer token. A Source Cooperative mirror (refreshed by hand, maintained by Development Seed) allows anonymous S3 listing of the manifest. Not advertised in CMR (CMR still points at the January 2026 proof of concept, also included here).\n\nStatus (probed 2026-11-06): Experimental snapshot; pipeline pushed 2026-11-05; Source Coop mirror 2026-10-15.",
